; EzyMap Scalp Mastery V2.1b - EzyMap_V2_1b_FULL.set
; FULL V2.1b - both stages active. Cumulative: S01+S02. These are also the
; compiled-in DEFAULTS, so this file is redundant with a fresh binary; it
; exists so the A/B pair is symmetric and so the intended values are explicit
; in the tester rather than implied.
;
; S01 (InpZeroConfAllowCurrentMapTier=false): the CURRENT_MAP / CURRENT_OUTER
; tier is excluded from the ladder, and CURRENT_OUTER's directional override
; and retire-on-fill privileges go with it. Scored sources become W1_CLUSTER,
; W1_SINGLE, D1_H4_CLUSTER, D1_SINGLE, LOW_RISK, READY. H4_SINGLE stays at
; priority 7, unchanged.
;
; S02 (InpZeroConfIncludeLevel1=false): the four W1/D1 ladder loops start at
; index 1, so only the OUTER level (S2/D2) can trigger. H4 is unaffected on
; both counts - the H4_SINGLE loop still runs both levels and h4[0]/h4[1] stay
; available as cluster partners. LOW_RISK and READY are untouched.
;
; Only the V2.1b S01-S02 inputs are listed. Load this ON TOP of your V2.1a
; working set - every other input keeps its current value.
;
; Expect FEWER zero-conf fills than STAGE0. Compare trade count first and
; expectancy second, and slice the CSV by trigger type: the whole point is
; that the surviving six sources should carry a better win rate than the
; nine-source mix did.
;
; Confirm from the OnInit log that you loaded it. This file must produce:
;   V2.1b: CURRENT_MAP/CURRENT_OUTER tier disabled ...
;   V2.1b: W1/D1 triggers restricted to S2/D2 (Level2) only ...
;
InpZeroConfAllowCurrentMapTier=false
InpZeroConfIncludeLevel1=false
